Now that data exists in your cluster, you can search for it. For example, you might want to search
for all root vegetables, or get a count of all leafy greens, or ﬁnd the number of errors logged per
hour.
Basic searches
A basic search looks something like this:
GET veggies/_search?q=name:l*
The request produces a JSON response that contains the lettuce document.
Advanced searches
You can perform more advanced searches by providing the query options as JSON in the request
body:
GET veggies/_search
{
"query": {
"term": {
"name": "lettuce"
}
}
}
